{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing","id":1039049,"title":"Potion Brewing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-27T12:30:52-08:00","id":1039049,"title":"Potion Brewing","content":"I've been thinking about brewing potions in Mage. I assume that a potion can be used as the focus instrument for an effect such as Life 3 attribute boosting where each success on the Arete roll can increase an attribute by one or, if using the dividing successes rule could be used to increase duration instead.<br /> <br /> However could an alchemist mage brew a potion beforehand and by using the extended rolls rules for rites garner a whole bunch of successes imbued into the potion so that whoever drinks it later gets the attribute boost?<br /> <br /> Assuming that's reasonable, and doesn't need any other spheres (except maybe Matter to 'bind' it to the liquid), would it be sensible to require the mage to spend some of those successes on how long the potion stays fresh?<br /> <br /> i.e. If the alchemist manages to accrue a total of 8 successes when brewing the potion could he dedicate 5 to increasing the attribute, 1 to the duration (= one scene), and 2 to the length of time before it 'goes off'' (= one day)?<br /> <br /> Would that make brewing potions too useful? and what penalties does someone who has drunk such a potion have? I assume it would count as an ongoing effect thus increasing the difficulty of further effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:43:43-08:00","id":1039056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing#post1039049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However could an alchemist mage brew a potion beforehand and by using the extended rolls rules for rites garner a whole bunch of successes imbued into the potion so that whoever drinks it later gets the attribute boost?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That would be making an artefact and would require Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:23:51-08:00","id":1039078,"title":"","content":"I remember reading something about Alchemy in Sorcerers Crusade.<br /> IIRC<br /> The person who imbibed the potion gets poisoned, unless the mage was present (and his Arete) in that case the potion worked as intended.<br /> Maybe there is more.<br /> Otherwise:<br /> You could get it with Prime 2 with appropriate tass.<br /> <br /> Time 4 with the trigger being drinking the potion.<br /> <br /> Prime 4 and an Artifact-bottle transforming every suitable liquid placed inside into an potion with the desired effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:25:00-08:00","id":1039079,"title":"","content":"So what would be the right system for creating a one shot artefact like a potion? I'm using the 20th anniversary rules and they're pretty light when it comes to making Wonders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:00:41-08:00","id":1039092,"title":"","content":"The most up to date source would be Forged by Dragons Fire","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:32:41-08:00","id":1039113,"title":"","content":"M20 states that you can make &quot;temporary artefacts&quot; with Prime 3, but doesn't really elaborate on this much, instead saying &quot;wait till Book of Secrets!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Revised has it that you can make Charms (Artefacts with charges) at Prime 2, and this would be the main way I'd expect for potions to work. Each point would represent a single portion, and successes rolled would be standard Artefact rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T15:28:27-08:00","id":1039135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039113#post1039113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 states that you can make &amp;quot;temporary artefacts&amp;quot; with Prime 3, but doesn't really elaborate on this much, instead saying &amp;quot;wait till Book of Secrets!!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Revised has it that you can make Charms (Artefacts with charges) at Prime 2, and this would be the main way I'd expect for potions to work. Each point would represent a single portion, and successes rolled would be standard Artefact rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Dragons Fire and Revised, you can make with Prime 3 if you have Tass with the adequate ressonance. With Prime 4, it doesn't matter the ressonance (same goes for all Prime effects - adequate ressonance for Charms - Prime 2; otherwise, Prime 3, and so on)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T16:49:27-08:00","id":1039157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039135#post1039135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Dragons Fire and Revised, you can make with Prime 3 if you have Tass with the adequate ressonance. With Prime 4, it doesn't matter the ressonance (same goes for all Prime effects - adequate ressonance for Charms - Prime 2; otherwise, Prime 3, and so on)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought is was Prime 3 with Tass, Prime 4 with Quint, but the ressonance always matters since it will usually lead to associated effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T18:57:41-08:00","id":1039201,"title":"","content":"You could make Charms that are very similar to what your are trying to do<br /> <br /> Nevermind already stated. Sorry half asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T19:02:26-08:00","id":1039208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039157#post1039157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought is was Prime 3 with Tass, Prime 4 with Quint, but the ressonance always matters since it will usually lead to associated effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I guess you're right.<br /> <br /> I have a question thou, can Prime be used to shape ressonance? Because if it can, that's pointless anyway<br /> <br /> And I say it could, after all the Union always sanitize the Nodes they conquer (so, if they change nephandic nodes into &quot;neutral pattern&quot; ones...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T19:41:16-08:00","id":1039218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039208#post1039208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I guess you're right.<br /> <br /> I have a question thou, can Prime be used to shape ressonance? Because if it can, that's pointless anyway<br /> <br /> And I say it could, after all the Union always sanitize the Nodes they conquer (so, if they change nephandic nodes into &quot;neutral pattern&quot; ones...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance is more of a Mind thing. You probably need Prime and Mind to do things to resonance.<br /> <br /> Either that or make a Soulgem with Prime 4 which can change the resonance of any quintessence you hold into your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:31:15-08:00","id":1039238,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can &quot;attune&quot; the etherial emanations of things with Prime 1 or 2, I can't remember now, to make it easier to use Corr effects (and if you attune an object or living being to you, you don't need to spend 1 succes to hit the target, it's like using the effect on the Mage himself). So, Prime manipulate the etherial energies; mind manipulate the &quot;psichic energy&quot;. I guess one is the consequence of the other<br /> <br /> I use Prime 1 for atunement to make magikal tracking devices. You can also blood Bond someone (yep, like vampires), using Prime 2 to &quot;adjust&quot; the target to yourself... Making him think about you the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T22:35:42-08:00","id":1039266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039056#post1039056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. That would be making an artefact and would require Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I dare say there *is* a way to make potions work without them being wonders, or using time 4: Simply through the Mage's belief and handling it as a sort of hanging ritual, no different than any other focusing of an effect and taking the last steps of the ritual when it's time to kick things into gear.<br /> <br /> There are two caveats to this of course:<br /> <br /> 1) It's like a hanging ritual; Nothing else can be cast in the meanwhile, lest it's aborted. That means you can only have one single working potion at once, rules-wise. This works well along the lines of <i>'It is a fickle thing, this potion, and should be consumed as soon as possible lest it spoils'</i><br /> 2) The potion only works on themself or if the mage *witnesses* it being drunk by someone else and has used the appropriate spheres to affect others. It is not an item that anybody can take with them and use whenever they like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T23:34:42-08:00","id":1039282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039266#post1039266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, I dare say there *is* a way to make potions work without them being wonders, or using time 4: Simply through the Mage's belief and handling it as a sort of hanging ritual, no different than any other focusing of an effect and taking the last steps of the ritual when it's time to kick things into gear.<br /> <br /> There are two caveats to this of course:<br /> <br /> 1) It's like a hanging ritual; Nothing else can be cast in the meanwhile, lest it's aborted. That means you can only have one single working potion at once, rules-wise. This works well along the lines of <i>'It is a fickle thing, this potion, and should be consumed as soon as possible lest it spoils'</i><br /> 2) The potion only works on themself or if the mage *witnesses* it being drunk by someone else and has used the appropriate spheres to affect others. It is not an item that anybody can take with them and use whenever they like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested in this hanging ritual thing.<br /> Is this RAW? Just curious, I steal it right away for my Alchemist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:45:40-08:00","id":1039562,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit disappointed in how most of the interpretations demand higher level spheres, I was thinking that brewing potions would be something less experienced mages would be able to do. By the time you get to Prime 4/Time 4 (as well as your primary spheres) most mages don't really need to be messing about with brewing potions as I'd expect them to create effects with far fewer Arete rolls than before. Feels like a neglected option in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T13:10:53-08:00","id":1039573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039562#post1039562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit disappointed in how most of the interpretations demand higher level spheres, I was thinking that brewing potions would be something less experienced mages would be able to do. By the time you get to Prime 4/Time 4 (as well as your primary spheres) most mages don't really need to be messing about with brewing potions as I'd expect them to create effects with far fewer Arete rolls than before. Feels like a neglected option in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf's Mage doesn't really represent <i>any</i> of the &quot;real&quot; magic systems. Because &quot;real&quot; magic systems are all based around theater and ceremony and take hours of time and that doesn't make for fun RPG experience. Mage magic works on a turn scale, in seconds, and that means many things get left on the roadside. The ability to pre-make your spellcasting rolls in a safe place would actually be extremely powerful in Mage. It's much better to do a long ritual and get yourself a bandolier of fire flasks with five successes each and already blown paradox than it is to roll your three Arete to throw a fireball in combat, with a potentially great risk of being fucked by paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T13:59:47-08:00","id":1039589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039282#post1039282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm interested in this hanging ritual thing.<br /> Is this RAW? Just curious, I steal it right away for my Alchemist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> RAW describes how rituals can take time, and can be left off and picked up again until finish. It stands to reason that the ritual starting with preparing the potion's ingredients, to brewing it, to finally ingesting it could be cut up the same way. But, see the caveats above <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It wouldn't provide the advantages of being a wonder or hung spell, but it would allow something like potions without super high spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T23:12:35-08:00","id":1039842,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11490_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11490\" data-vbnamecard=\"11490\">Dogstar</a> You can also just use a potion as instrument, in this case you roll Arete at the time the potion is imbibed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T00:20:39-08:00","id":1039862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039266#post1039266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The potion only works on themself or if the mage *witnesses* it being drunk by someone else and has used the appropriate spheres to affect others. It is not an item that anybody can take with them and use whenever they like.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if you add Correspondence?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T05:50:34-08:00","id":1039948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039862#post1039862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you add Correspondence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean.<br /> The thing is, since this is not a wonder, nor an already cast spell, the Mage needs to witness the potion being drunk in order for the final Arete roll.<br /> I don't think Correspondence can help in this case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:29:56-08:00","id":1040620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039948#post1039948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what you mean.<br /> The thing is, since this is not a wonder, nor an already cast spell, the Mage needs to witness the potion being drunk in order for the final Arete roll.<br /> I don't think Correspondence can help in this case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The potion is cast when somebody drinks it; then Arete is rolled and consequences follow. Correspondence allows this even if the Mage is not there. From where do you get the need for Mage to witness the drinking?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also - can an Iteration-Xer create a timed bomb without Time 4? :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:06:00-08:00","id":1040646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040620#post1040620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The potion is cast when somebody drinks it; then Arete is rolled and consequences follow. Correspondence allows this even if the Mage is not there. From where do you get the need for Mage to witness the drinking?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing: The potion is not cast when somebody drinks it. The potion is cast when the Mage witnesses somebody drinking it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That's the big difference when it's not a wonder or using time 4. It's not the act of drinking the potion activates the effect. it's the Mage witnessing the potion being drunk that activates the effect. If somebody away from the Mage drinks the potion, absolutely nothing happens. No Artete roll, nada.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also - can an Iteration-Xer create a timed bomb without Time 4? :&gt; </div> </div> </div>Yes, by using properties of Life or Matter patterns that degrade at a specific speed - just like normal time bombs. The Arete rolls and effect are done long before the bomb actually explodes - but at this point I don't really see a point in this, as the explosion itself would be quite normal. Just the 'fuse', so to speak, would have been a magickal effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-30-2017, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:25:26-08:00","id":1040653,"title":"","content":"Maybe I am missing something or maybe this idea is already mentioned in another way that I didn't catch but I thought the following scenarios were both true.<br /> <br /> 1) Using Life 3 to create a healing effect that uses a liquid in a bottle as the instrument would require the obersavtion of the liquid being consumed, with the only/final Arete roll made at that point. Time 4 to make a contingency effect like normal. Correspondence 3 for long distance like normal, etc, etc. This is the method that most people have been talking about.<br /> <br /> 2. Using Life 3, Matter 3 to lock an effect to turn the liquid inside into a substance that has the effect on the human body to greatly speed up healing if applied in the correct method (drinking, injecting, breathing vapors, applied topically to wound site, etc.) The EFFECT is cast on the liquid, spending successes for duration for the shelf life of the potion and for the effectiveness of the healing. The GAME BENEFIT MECHANIC is the health levels regained when the potion is applied. The potion is worthless if not stored safely, isapplied in the wrong way or applied on something that isn't the intended target (I.e. not a human or maybe not that SPECIFIC human). Once the potion is used, the magic locking the effect no longer has a valid target (the substance itself has been changed too much) and unravels.<br /> <br /> The upside of this second method is that initiate magi could do it, but then there is a game balance question of churning out potions. Even if the effect (at the time of casting) is vulgar, a successful casting still only gets 1 paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:26:40-08:00","id":1040655,"title":"","content":"Potions not working unless the Mage is there is a point made by the Progenitor in their revised Convetion Book.<br /> &quot;<i>Healing waters recovered from the Node your people took from us. (...) Destined for our clinic downtown. We're only trying to help people here, can't you psychopaths see that?</i>&quot;<br /> (...) &quot;<i>And when you're not here to administer the treatment, sweetie? What then? When they slather the salves, burn the incense, and drink the irradiated water... is it going to mend them? Or just make them more sick? The superstitious bullshit you peddle is not medicine.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040646#post1040646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing: The potion is not cast when somebody drinks it. The potion is cast when the Mage witnesses somebody drinking it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That's the big difference when it's not a wonder or using time 4. It's not the act of drinking the potion activates the effect. it's the Mage witnessing the potion being drunk that activates the effect. If somebody away from the Mage drinks the potion, absolutely nothing happens. No Artete roll, nada.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where it is written that True Magick works like this - &quot;It's the Mage witnessing the potion being drunk that activates the effect.&quot; ?<br /> <br /> If you add Correspondence 3, you can make it so that, when somebody drinks it, the Mage either sees or otherwise feels that the potion is drunk - hence he witnesses it. The potion counts as a perfect connection, so at most one additional success would be needed to do this. Would this work? The potion or the container could be prepared specially for this.<br /> Or it might be that the mind-set of a potion-maker with knowledge of Correspondence is enough to make a potion work like this. &quot;My elixirs are a part of me distilled into a mixture...once you realize this, it follows that I can no more be unaware of someone drinking one, than I would be unaware of that person shaking my hand. Thus my Enlightenment works through my potions, wherever they are.&quot;<br /> Also, I think Correspondence 2, or even 1, might be enough - considering that the use here is not on the one drinking the potion, but on the potion so that the Mage is aware when it is being drunk. Maybe Prime 1 Correspondence 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040646#post1040646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, by using properties of Life or Matter patterns that degrade at a specific speed - just like normal time bombs. The Arete rolls and effect are done long before the bomb actually explodes - but at this point I don't really see a point in this, as the explosion itself would be quite normal. Just the 'fuse', so to speak, would have been a magickal effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's good to hear this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-30-2017, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T09:42:51-08:00","id":1040725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you add Correspondence 3, you can make it so that, when somebody drinks it, the Mage either sees or otherwise feels that the potion is drunk - hence he witnesses it. </div> </div> </div>Stop.<br /> <br /> This implies that an effect is already finished and cast. This implies that the potion already uses Time 4 to trigger the correspondence effect as soon as somebody drinks it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> In that case you don't *need* a correspondence effect at all, because you can just use Life 3 + Time 4 when making the potion and be done with it. Time 4 makes the Life effect trigger on drinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040655#post1040655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where it is written that True Magick works like this - &quot;It's the Mage witnessing the potion being drunk that activates the effect.&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because we are trying to find a way of making the potion work without using Time 4 or making the potion a Wonder, nor is the person drinking the potion supposed to be the one rolling Arete (or even a Mage).<br /> <br /> Without Time 4, the supernatural healing kicks in as soon as the last Arete roll for the effect gets rolled, which the Mage who made the potion has to roll when the potion is drunk.<br /> The only way that Mage would roll the last Arete roll of the whole potion-preparation-then-drinking ritual would be if they witness the potion being consumed.<br /> And without Time 4, you can't trigger any correspondence effect as soon as somebody starts drinking the potion while far away, thus that last Arete roll wouldn't happen unless the Mage is present.<br /> <br /> I hope that explains the problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-30-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T10:02:10-08:00","id":1040736,"title":"","content":"Ok, so from what I can gather here there are about 4 ways to create a &quot;delayed effect&quot;.<br /> <br /> 1. Good ol' Time 4 with a dash of Entropy 1 for the famous Programmed Event rote<br /> 2. Prime 2/3/4 for Charms/Artefacts/talismans that are capable of doing the effect all on their own (which Prime level it is depends on which rules you read).<br /> 3. The Hermetic &quot;Everything but the last step&quot; stuff, where all the prep work is done ahead of time to build the effect, only to be set of later.<br /> 4. Entropy 1 with various Life, Matter, and Forces patterns under the Technocratic Paradigm of Rates of Decay.<br /> <br /> This is how I see these four methods differ descriptively as well as mechanically<br /> <br /> 1.<br /> D: The Mage has cast an effect and froze it in time, only to go off if certain events come to pass. Whether it be by asking Angels to keep the event on hold, causing a flux around the time stream, or simply zapping an effect forward in time, the effect has been cast and will happen later.<br /> <br /> M: Mage needs Time 4 as a minimum, Any other sphere can be used to determine when the effect will break (if not at a specific time) such as &quot;Break when the wind changes&quot; with Forces 1, or &quot;Break when a spirit walks by&quot; with Spirit 1. But Entropy 1 is usually the go to sphere for this, since it can be a lot more versatile and can encompass things like &quot;break on utterance of the password, break upon my death, break when Jenkins falls asleep&quot; and so forth.<br /> <br /> Arete is rolled at the point of casting, with all parameters determined before (or during) the ritual, subject to successes. This is probably the most versatile of these methods described, as well as the simplest to operate, not requiring the mage witness the results for them to happen. But it comes at the steep price of requiring Time 4.<br /> <br /> 2.<br /> D: The mage crafts a tool capable of either doing a specific kind of spell, be it only for a limited number of charges, or permanently. While the full scope of Wonders are too vast to state here, the Mage is essentially crafting a piece of their paradigm into a static object or dynamic life pattern (assuming other spheres aren't being used). The Wonder crafted is often an extension of the mage's beliefs, and thus may work independently of the mage themselves. The magic is now a (perhaps) permanent feature of the object imbued.<br /> <br /> M: Prime of various kinds is required. Which Prime is required for what types of Wonder differs depending on whether you go with Revised of M20 rules. The technique of crafting them also differs, but suffice to say this cannot be done &quot;on a whim&quot;. You will need a substantial amount of quintessence (possibly in the form of Tass) as well as a innate knowledge of what you are trying to craft (want an enchanted sword? Better call a Blacksmith). Once crafted, the Wonder will function reliably for as long as it is required to, and possibly indefinitely. Providing the material components are met, and the great number of successes is achieved, sometimes higher than 20 or 30, then the wonder is good to go.<br /> <br /> Arete is rolled at the point of crafting, and can be one of the most convoluted Ritual Magic Rolls an earthbound player will ever do in their life. The upside is you've made a magic item that doesn't your supervision to function. The type of Wonder made will determine the limitations, but for the most part the magic is done once the wonder is made. This has the added benefit over the Programmed Event rote of your mage not needing to keep the effect in place, which may otherwise hamper their ability to do magic along the way. The downside is that anyone with the correct paradigm will be able to use these Wonders for whatever they want, and having Wonders stolen is a staple of so many campaigns.<br /> <br /> Also, Resonance. But I'm not going to get into that here.<br /> <br /> 3.<br /> D: In theory, this can be done with any sphere at any level, all it requires is a good high ritual and knowing what you'll be doing for it. The Mage may set up all their equipment and start drawing Seals of Solomon but leave out one last line. They may start praying to the spirits to imbue a certain word with powers only released once the word is uttered with intent, they may begin an elaborate song and leave all but the last note. They may be charging up their Tesla coils within their Lightning Blasters, and waiting for the right time to strike. The point is the ritual is started and built, but not concluded, so the effect is ready, but waiting to be triggered.<br /> <br /> M: Unlike the techniques above, the spheres aren't so much the concern as the timing of it all, and this technique may not be compatible with all paradigms. An Ecstatic who believes you have to be &quot;in the moment&quot; for magic to work, for example, might not think it's possible to enter and exit &quot;the moment&quot; so easily. Either you do it while you're high, or you're not really doing it at all.<br /> <br /> The rules on how this works are not fully stated, so everything here is up to interpretation, but this is how I imagine it working:<br /> - At the point of Ritual, the Mage will make a number of Mundane style rolls.<br /> - The difficulty will be determined by how complicated the magic effect they want to create is. Arete is rolled once the &quot;final step&quot; is put in place.<br /> - Successes during the Mundane rolls will determine how many Arete rolls you are allowed at the &quot;final step&quot; part, and will be proportional with the highest sphere rating within the effect.<br /> <br /> So, if you were doing a Forces 3 effect to cause light to turn into fire. Every 3 successes in the mundane Ritual roll would equal 1 Arete roll at the time of the Final Step.<br /> <br /> I imagine there will be a few caveats.<br /> <br /> - The Ritual will take a lot of time to perform, and the mage will need their full concentration on the ritual for the entire duration. If they are distracted at any point, then the entire thing fails. Also, they would only be able to create one hanging effect per ritual. i.e. if you wanted to Charge up your blaster's tesla coil, you would have to wait until it's &quot;fully charged&quot; before you can then go and &quot;charge&quot; your Gravity Gun.<br /> - Regardless of how you perform your ritual, it will be exhausting. The longer you try to go at it, the more Stamina rolls you will need to succeed to keep going.<br /> - The effect is fixed when the ritual is complete, this includes which spheres are what levels are involved, as well as what is being manipulated. Things like the location of your teleportation, the form of the animal you will turn into, Whether you're chucking Thunderbolts or Lightning, all of that must be decided now and cannot be changed.<br /> - Other things, such as how many targets, duration of the effect once cast, and damage produced, can be decided after the Arete roll as normal.<br /> - You have to roll every Arete roll you accumulate at the point of the Final Step with the difficulty determined as though you were doing an extended ritual (because, you did). Rules for Difficulty and Paradox are the same there.<br /> <br /> This means if you somehow Ritual yourself 10 Arete rolls, you have to roll ALL TEN ARETE ROLLS, and suffer the consequences as they happen.<br /> <br /> - These effects cannot hang indefinitely without the aid of Time 4 (by which point you might as well just make it a Programmed Effect). For every day the after the initial ritual the final step is not implemented, 1 arete roll is lost. The potency of the ritual decays over time. (perhaps you could strengthen this with Entropy 5 and Prime something, or maybe Time 3 and Prime something).<br /> <br /> The bonuses of this is that a lot of the work of a ritual has already been done ahead of time. So all you need do is roll your Arete at the point of the Final Step and Wizz Bang, Magick! Another benefit is, depending on how the mage's paradigm works, you don't necessarily have to be the on to do the Final Step. After charging your gun, someone else can pull the trigger, after enchanting a specific word, someone else can call it (with intent). It is still the Mage's Arete that gets rolled, and the Mage in question has to be in the room and aware of what's just happened. Also they need to believe that what's just happened has happened. (so if you don't say the magic word with enough Gusto in your voice, the casting Mage may not think it would be enough.) What you gain in time, however, you lose in adaptability. The effect is set at the point of ritual and cannot be changed without dismissing the effect entirely.<br /> <br /> 4.<br /> D: In many ways, this is not unlike the 3rd technique, but with a little added twist, the technocrat does not need to observe the effect occur in order for it to occur. This technique only works because the Technocrat is able to rely on the consensus to observe it for them. In areas where the Technocracy's Science does not work, this too will be ineffectual. But it will work incredibly accurately in &quot;lab conditions&quot;. The Technocrat need only set up their apparatus to, say, observe the rate of decay of a radioactive substance, and have the procedure set itself off once the radiation has dipped bellow a specific level.<br /> <br /> M: Requires Entropy 1 to sense and measure Rate of Decay, and one of the other Pattern Spheres to know what is being sensed, be it Enzymes (Life) Radiation (Forces) or Chemical Clock Reactions (Matter). Mechanically speaking, this allows the Technocrat to not require Time 4 to do their delayed procedures. Such is one of the benefits of working with the Technocratic Consensus. In theory, other mages may be able to create similar effects if they can find a piece of reality that is open to their paradigm. But such places are usually pretty difficult to come by. Even the Etherites may not be able to rely on these techniques since their brand of Science! tends to fall apart the moment they leave the room.<br /> <br /> <br /> So here's how a Potion would be brewed with the above techniques:<br /> <br /> 1. Your Potions are simply bottled effects. The very effect itself is stored in time, held within the liquid, only to be unleashed at the point of drinking.<br /> 2. Your Potions contain magical liquids imbued with powerful magics. They will function for as long as there is still juice in the bottle. (I imagine these will be Charm type temporary Wonders)<br /> 3. Your Potions are how you do your magic. You brew them and once you drink them, or throw them to the ground, they come into effect.<br /> 4. Potions? What are you talking about? This is a carefully constructed Solution which will have corrosive properties the moment the reaction is left to settle. I added a substrate which will turn the liquid blue to let us know once the solution is ready to administer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-30-2017, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:09:52-08:00","id":1040833,"title":"","content":"Saikou, thanks for providing an list of options, but I have a question about one of them in particular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040736#post1040736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.<br /> D: The mage crafts a tool capable of either doing a specific kind of spell, be it only for a limited number of charges, or permanently. While the full scope of Wonders are too vast to state here, the Mage is essentially crafting a piece of their paradigm into a static object or dynamic life pattern (assuming other spheres aren't being used). The Wonder crafted is often an extension of the mage's beliefs, and thus may work independently of the mage themselves. The magic is now a (perhaps) permanent feature of the object imbued.<br /> <br /> M: Prime of various kinds is required. Which Prime is required for what types of Wonder differs depending on whether you go with Revised of M20 rules. The technique of crafting them also differs, but suffice to say this cannot be done &quot;on a whim&quot;. You will need a substantial amount of quintessence (possibly in the form of Tass) as well as a innate knowledge of what you are trying to craft (want an enchanted sword? Better call a Blacksmith). Once crafted, the Wonder will function reliably for as long as it is required to, and possibly indefinitely. Providing the material components are met, and the great number of successes is achieved, sometimes higher than 20 or 30, then the wonder is good to go.<br /> <br /> Arete is rolled at the point of crafting, and can be one of the most convoluted Ritual Magic Rolls an earthbound player will ever do in their life. The upside is you've made a magic item that doesn't your supervision to function. The type of Wonder made will determine the limitations, but for the most part the magic is done once the wonder is made. This has the added benefit over the Programmed Event rote of your mage not needing to keep the effect in place, which may otherwise hamper their ability to do magic along the way. The downside is that anyone with the correct paradigm will be able to use these Wonders for whatever they want, and having Wonders stolen is a staple of so many campaigns.<br /> <br /> Also, Resonance. But I'm not going to get into that here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The root of the question comes down to what is the difference between a Wonder/Charm/Talisman/other nomenclature for enchanted item and an effect that is locked onto an object that doesn't affect the object itself in anyway, but does affect other things near it?<br /> <br /> For example, if a mage uses Force 3, Matter 3 to heat up a piece of metal and keep it heated for days at a time (appropriate to the duration), that could easily be handled as a locked effect. Granted, the mage would need to be careful that the piece of metal doesn't get too hot to deform its shape, and that whatever it is resting on or held in doesn't catch fire, but again a simple of effect. The game mechanic of that effect would be the heat that the piece of metal gives off (i.e. it keeps you warm if kept nearby, but it really hurts if held or used as a weapon).<br /> <br /> Same thing for a Matter 3 effect, locked, to make a trench coat act as better armor. The effect is to make the trench coat more durable, but the game mechanic would be a bonus to the Armor Rating of the person wearing it.<br /> <br /> Why would these work as locked effects and not need to be enchanted items? Is it because they are constant effects and not effects that activate, run their course and then die off?<br /> <br /> If so, would it not stand to reason that creating a Life 3, Matter 3 effect in a liquid that greatly assists the body's natural healing also work as a locked effect? The effect itself is distorting the liquid, but the game mechanic benefit would be the health levels gained when that liquid interacts with a wounded human body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12655,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","user":"tzizimine","date":". 01-30-2017, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:25:54-08:00","id":1040847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzizimine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040833#post1040833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saikou, thanks for providing an list of options, but I have a question about one of them in particular.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The root of the question comes down to what is the difference between a Wonder/Charm/Talisman/other nomenclature for enchanted item and an effect that is locked onto an object that doesn't affect the object itself in anyway, but does affect other things near it?<br /> <br /> For example, if a mage uses Force 3, Matter 3 to heat up a piece of metal and keep it heated for days at a time (appropriate to the duration), that could easily be handled as a locked effect. Granted, the mage would need to be careful that the piece of metal doesn't get too hot to deform its shape, and that whatever it is resting on or held in doesn't catch fire, but again a simple of effect. The game mechanic of that effect would be the heat that the piece of metal gives off (i.e. it keeps you warm if kept nearby, but it really hurts if held or used as a weapon).<br /> <br /> Same thing for a Matter 3 effect, locked, to make a trench coat act as better armor. The effect is to make the trench coat more durable, but the game mechanic would be a bonus to the Armor Rating of the person wearing it.<br /> <br /> Why would these work as locked effects and not need to be enchanted items? Is it because they are constant effects and not effects that activate, run their course and then die off?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The distinction is simple.<br /> <br /> A Wonder is capable of casting the spell at the command of its wielder. If you were to simply enchanted a Sword with Forces 3 Matter 3 alone then yes, the metal would heat and its thrust will burn. But this would be an ongoing effect held up by the Mage who cast it. They would need to put successes into duration to keep it lasting, and then would need to maintain the effect indefinitely until it runs out or they ultimately dismiss it. Each time the Mage created their effect, they would have to roll arete.<br /> <br /> To compose a Wonder out of the sword, however, you would be able to have the sword heat up on command, perhaps if one was to hold it up to the sky and recite a Latin phrase, it would then burst into flames, shutting off again when the user was finished. This would be possible to do multiple times without need of further Arete rolls. Furthermore, anyone who believed in the power of God and the use of Latin to invoke their favour, as well as the power the Wonder held, would be able to have the sword reveal its flame, even if they were a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> Matter effects on their own can create new materials, and indeed these would be fixed onto the matter patter it was assigned to. After all, Matter is static. The clothing wouldn't be enchanted so much as altered. It would be the difference between building a Fire Ward with Forces into your coat and transforming the material of your coat into something flame retardant.<br /> <br /> Paradox would not accumulate in the Wonder itself unless it carried its own Arete or supply of Quintessence. And then it depends on the magic being done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-30-2017, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:38:04-08:00","id":1040859,"title":"","content":"Thanks,<br /> <br /> Ok, so if the distinction between a Wonder/Talisman/etc, and a locked effect is <u>activated vs. sustained</u>, then creating an activate-use healing potion would be a Wonder/Talisman/etc, but then that raises a question about sustained effects that improve healing.<br /> <br /> For example, a Life 3 / Matter 3 to lock an effect into a &quot;Comfy Blanket&quot; to allow healing times for Lethal damage to be treated as healing times for Bashing (i.e. muuuuch quicker).<br /> <br /> What would be an appropriate success-effect ratio for something, in your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12655,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","user":"tzizimine","date":". 01-30-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:08:39-08:00","id":1040882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzizimine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040859#post1040859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks,<br /> <br /> Ok, so if the distinction between a Wonder/Talisman/etc, and a locked effect is <u>activated vs. sustained</u>, then creating an activate-use healing potion would be a Wonder/Talisman/etc, but then that raises a question about sustained effects that improve healing.<br /> <br /> For example, a Life 3 / Matter 3 to lock an effect into a &quot;Comfy Blanket&quot; to allow healing times for Lethal damage to be treated as healing times for Bashing (i.e. muuuuch quicker).<br /> <br /> What would be an appropriate success-effect ratio for something, in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, you can have &quot;sustained&quot; effects on Wonders as well. They just take a bit more time and Quintessence to create. Life 3 Prime 3/4/whatever would be able to make such a blanket and it would work for anyone who used it.<br /> <br /> The locked effect, however, would only work for as long as the Mage kept it running. Also, what exactly would be the point of this? You have Life 3, just turn the Lethal into Bashing yourself, or better yet get rid of it completely with a Vulgar move. Sometimes a little Paradox is worth not being on Death's door.<br /> <br /> Something to point out. Healing can only ever be cast one someone once per scene. So having a continuous healing effect is rather pointless in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:17:39-08:00","id":1040891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040882#post1040882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, you can have &quot;sustained&quot; effects on Wonders as well. They just take a bit more time and Quintessence to create. Life 3 Prime 3/4/whatever would be able to make such a blanket and it would work for anyone who used it.<br /> <br /> The locked effect, however, would only work for as long as the Mage kept it running. Also, what exactly would be the point of this? You have Life 3, just turn the Lethal into Bashing yourself, or better yet get rid of it completely with a Vulgar move. Sometimes a little Paradox is worth not being on Death's door.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, 1) I wouldn't want it has a Wonder, simply because that is more expensive to make and 2) If I needed to use healing for a handful of mundanes over time, this method is going to attract less attention that their wounds suddenly closing on their own and less risk of me botching a roll here or there and 3) If I already racked up enough Paradox to worry for my life, have a back-up plan is pretty smart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040882#post1040882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something to point out. Healing can only ever be cast one someone once per scene. So having a continuous healing effect is rather pointless in and of itself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can you provide a reference to this rule? I don't remember seeing this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:41:31-08:00","id":1040906,"title":"","content":"Well, quite simply put, If it isn't a wonder, then it's going to run out of juice eventually. I'd say each success you put into your blanket would be split between potency and Duration. When duration runs out, the whole thing becomes inert. Potency will determine how many levels it will be able to heal in total. Once that runs out the entire thing becomes inert. Then you'll have to recast.<br /> <br /> Also, you can turn Lethal into Bashin coincidentally, just cast it before you examine the wound. &quot;oh look, it was just a flesh wound&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mage Revised: pp.168: &quot;Note that when a mage alters or heals a Pattern, she does so to the limit of her capabilities. If a mage pulls off a Life Effect, she cannot recast the same Effect for more successes until the Pattern has undergone some natural change (that is, a change of scene). Thus, the mage can transform herself and then change differently or change back, but if she heals an injury or causes a wound in a given scene, she cannot use that power on the same subject again - she's done all that she can to the Pattern at the time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:14:24-08:00","id":1040932,"title":"","content":"Is that same rule in M20? It looks like it was omitted (sorry don't have a copy of Revised).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T16:55:24-08:00","id":1040973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzizimine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040932#post1040932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that same rule in M20? It looks like it was omitted (sorry don't have a copy of Revised).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having trouble finding it, but then M20's Sphere chapter leaves a lot to be desired. There is nowhere in the book that discusses how Healing works, and HDYDT assumes that because it's in the Common Magickal Feats table it's not worth discussing.<br /> <br /> However, there is a similar passage in Mage 2e, which leads me to believe that this is an intended limitation of the Life sphere, and its omission from M20 was not to remove it.<br /> <br /> Mage 2e pp.202: &quot;Each attempt at healing a Pattern assumes that the mage does as much restorative work as she is able. Repeating the Effect will not heal more damage. At the Storyteller's discretion, the mage may attempt to fix more Pattern damage after the creature has had sufficient time to heal. Any new damage suffered by the subject can also be treated by the mage. Some sorcerers have been known to cure a little bit of damage, cause more and then try again. Of course, these same mages tend to botch this Effect and cause immense damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd say unless you can find somewhere where it explicitly states there is no limit to Heals, that this limitation carries over from the previous games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-30-2017, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:08:48-08:00","id":1040976,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. It just raises the question of 2+ mages attempting to heal separately. Does the attempt of one prevent the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:13:17-08:00","id":1040977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzizimine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040976#post1040976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense. It just raises the question of 2+ mages attempting to heal separately. Does the attempt of one prevent the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say so. The Life pattern is already healing itself. Give it time.<br /> <br /> I also rule than any effects such as giving yourself Extra Health Levels, or numbing yourself to the pain (ignoring loss of dice) with Life needs to be dismissed before you can heal since you're already affecting that Life pattern with this kind of magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:09:21-08:00","id":1041263,"title":"","content":"RAW speaks of a mage (as on one mage) to deduct from there that one healing from any mage prevents healing for the scene is a bit of a stretch.<br /> \u201cHaving problems with regenerating foes? Just heal 'em before you blast them!\u201c<br /> \u201cI am truly sorry, but since my student tried to heal you I am powerless to close this still fatal wound any further. Can I teleport someone to you, for last words?\u201c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:57:36-08:00","id":1041295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1041263#post1041263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW speaks of a mage (as on one mage) to deduct from there that one healing from any mage prevents healing for the scene is a bit of a stretch.<br /> \u201cHaving problems with regenerating foes? Just heal 'em before you blast them!\u201c<br /> \u201cI am truly sorry, but since my student tried to heal you I am powerless to close this still fatal wound any further. Can I teleport someone to you, for last words?\u201c</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I refer then to this line &quot;Any new damage suffered by the subject can also be treated by the mage. Some sorcerers have been known to cure a little bit of damage, cause more and then try again. Of course, these same mages tend to botch this Effect and cause immense damage.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T09:08:09-08:00","id":1041301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Each attempt at healing a Pattern assumes that the mage does as much restorative work as she is able. Repeating the Effect will not heal more damage. At the Storyteller's discretion, the mage may attempt to fix more Pattern damage after the creature has had sufficient time to heal. Any new damage suffered by the subject can also be treated by the mage. Some sorcerers have been known to cure a little bit of damage, cause more and then try again. Of course, these same mages tend to botch this Effect and cause immense damage.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To say that one mage &quot;does as much restorative work<b> as she is able</b>&quot; per each attempt at healing a Pattern doesn't mean that <i>another,</i> more powerful, mage shouldn't be able to heal more. On the contrary, one would assume that a more powerful mage it's able to heal more than a weaker one. In other words, the rule assumes that the mage did <i>as much restorative work as she is able</i>, that's why she can't heal more, not because the Pattern it's &quot;locked&quot; it never assumes that another mage can't do more<br /> <br /> One could argue that a mage can refuse to do &quot;as much restorative work as she is able&quot; (you get 3 successes, but decide that you don't want to heal the guy completely. One would assume that mages, who are supposed to be able to do anything, can choose to do this), thus being able to recast the heal (but only up to what she would have healed with 3 successes). To show how those words can be interpreted in a different way.<br /> <br /> Since the rule it's careful to mention that the mage that it's casting the effect it's doing so at the limit of<b> her </b>capabilities, and does not state that another mage shouldn't be able to try the effect, then it should be understood that these limits are those of the mage that casted the effect in the first place. Otherwise, yes, you could heal a single point of damage of a fatal wound to impede other mages from healing someone, or increase a mage's Strength 1 point, so the opponent can't increase it further. Which would be a oddly limmiting rule that would seem contrary to the spirit of what's written.<br /> <br /> In my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-31-2017, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T09:22:00-08:00","id":1041305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1041301#post1041301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To say that one mage &quot;does as much restorative work<b> as she is able</b>&quot; per each attempt at healing a Pattern doesn't mean that <i>another,</i> more powerful, mage shouldn't be able to heal more. On the contrary, one would assume that a more powerful mage it's able to heal more than a weaker one. In other words, the rule assumes that the mage did <i>as much restorative work as she is able</i>, that's why she can't heal more, not because the Pattern it's &quot;locked&quot; it never assumes that another mage can't do more<br /> <br /> One could argue that a mage can refuse to do &quot;as much restorative work as she is able&quot; (you get 3 successes, but decide that you don't want to heal the guy completely. One would assume that mages, who are supposed to be able to do anything, can choose to do this), thus being able to recast the heal (but only up to what she would have healed with 3 successes). To show how those words can be interpreted in a different way.<br /> <br /> Since the rule it's careful to mention that the mage that it's casting the effect it's doing so at the limit of<b> her </b>capabilities, and does not state that another mage shouldn't be able to try the effect, then it should be understood that these limits are those of the mage that casted the effect in the first place. Otherwise, yes, you could heal a single point of damage of a fatal wound to impede other mages from healing someone, or increase a mage's Strength 1 point, so the opponent can't increase it further. Which would be a oddly limmiting rule that would seem contrary to the spirit of what's written.<br /> <br /> In my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair point. In which case I'd add to it by saying that in order for another mage to come and provide additional healing, they'd have to meet and beat the original roll before more damage could be healed.<br /> <br /> So if Mage #1 has six levels of damage and heals four of them by rolling 2 successes. Mage #2 would be able to heal the final 2 levels of Mage #1 if they roll 4 successes (2 to meet Mage #1's roll, 1 to target non-self, and 1 to heal two bits of damage as per Damage and Duration).<br /> <br /> If, however, Mage #1 gets hurt before Mage #2 attempts the heal, then the slate is rubbed clean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T09:41:59-08:00","id":1041311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1041305#post1041305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fair point. In which case I'd add to it by saying that in order for another mage to come and provide additional healing, they'd have to meet and beat the original roll before more damage could be healed.<br /> <br /> So if Mage #1 has six levels of damage and heals four of them by rolling 2 successes. Mage #2 would be able to heal the final 2 levels of Mage #1 if they roll 4 successes (2 to meet Mage #1's roll, 1 to target non-self, and 1 to heal two bits of damage as per Damage and Duration).<br /> <br /> If, however, Mage #1 gets hurt before Mage #2 attempts the heal, then the slate is rubbed clean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something to this effect was my intention.<br /> As far as damaging something with Life, I would drop this restriction, because it would make other spheres stronger (especially Forces) unless you would place them under the same rule.<br /> <br /> Another thing to think of:<br /> If you didn't succeed in healing the damage in one go, you can make additional rolls at +1 difficulty each(still the same effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:00:08-08:00","id":1041316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1041311#post1041311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something to this effect was my intention.<br /> As far as damaging something with Life, I would drop this restriction, because it would make other spheres stronger (especially Forces) unless you would place them under the same rule.<br /> <br /> Another thing to think of:<br /> If you didn't succeed in healing the damage in one go, you can make additional rolls at +1 difficulty each(still the same effect).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you're getting at. Though the rules state outright that Forces <i>is </i>inherently stronger when it comes to dealing damage.<br /> <br /> It could be, however, that your mage's weighting in resonance bight have an effect on this. A Static Resonance would find it easier to heal, perhaps, while an Entropic resonance would find it easier to harm. This is all quite nebulous because resonance is nebulous by its very conceit, but it could be another thing to throw in there.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you are capable of healing others, you should also be capable of making yourself more sturdy and able to take hits, either by increasing soak dice (not necessarily increasing Stamina), or increasing your reflexes for avoiding or absorbing blows. There's more to Life than healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:40:50-08:00","id":1041939,"title":"","content":"Of course, if you want potions, it would probably be better to hire a Sorcerer with Alchemy to make you potions in exchange for stuff you can do better than the Sorcerer can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:13:51-08:00","id":1041952,"title":"","content":"I find the statement about Sorcerers being better at creating potions than Mages to be debatable. <br /> <br /> Alchemy it's vaguely described in the book, but I seem to remeber that you needed Alchemy 5, to mimic a supernatural power at level 2. That's not too powerful in my book. I don't think that a Sorcerer can make a potion to give you more than 2 actions per turn, much less a potion to time travel or turn you into a dragon.<br /> <br /> Alchemy 6 it's very impressive, but only because it can turn you into another splat and give you immortality, it doesn't do much in terms of the kind of potions you may want to use everyday. And it's a legendary trait that may be as rare as Archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:43:06-08:00","id":1042312,"title":"","content":"It seems unbalanced to me that one mage with Life 3 could meditate their way through an extended set of rolls every morning and boost their stats for the rest of the day while another mage with Life 3 cannot brew a potion that they can drink to boost their stats for 5 minutes that they can use anytime within the next week, unless they have a bunch of other spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T03:20:16-08:00","id":1042323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1042312#post1042312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems unbalanced to me that one mage with Life 3 could meditate their way through an extended set of rolls every morning and boost their stats for the rest of the day while another mage with Life 3 cannot brew a potion that they can drink to boost their stats for 5 minutes that they can use anytime within the next week, unless they have a bunch of other spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all mages are created equal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T06:44:43-08:00","id":1042381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1042312#post1042312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems unbalanced to me that one mage with Life 3 could meditate their way through an extended set of rolls every morning and boost their stats for the rest of the day while another mage with Life 3 cannot brew a potion that they can drink to boost their stats for 5 minutes that they can use anytime within the next week, unless they have a bunch of other spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real question is - at the time it is imbibed, does the power derive from the mage or from the potion? <br /> <br /> Consider a non-Life example. A Hermetic with Forces 3 might like to cast his fireballs by pointing a wand inscribed with the seven secret names of the archangel Gabriel. That's cool and all, and the wand gets him a bonus/lack of penalty on his roll as an appropriate magical tool/focus, but the wand itself is not doing the work - he is. If you mug that Hermetic in the street and take the wand, it does nothing when you point it. <br /> <br /> If that Hermetic wants to create a wand that <i>other people</i> could use, that's when Prime comes into it - because when others activate it, the power won't derive from him but rather from the wand itself. It's fundamentally different to throw fireballs than it is to create a tiny bit of a mage within a steel wand that can itself throw fireballs, which is why one needs Forces and the other needs Prime.<br /> <br /> So for potions - your Life 3 mage can totally create a special potion he keeps in a hip flask and imbibes to grant himself stat boosts, but the power is coming from him and not from the potion, and if he sells you that potion and you drink it a day later, it won't do anything because he's not there. Creating a potion that can cast a Life 3 effect on its own is different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:05:28-08:00","id":1042459,"title":"","content":"Thanks haldir, that states the issue much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:29:34-08:00","id":1042503,"title":"","content":"The issue with the two Life mages is allocating successes.<br /> If they use their successes the same way and the scene where the boosted stats are needed, then the mages are pretty much alike.<br /> <br /> But the Alchemist may think \u201cI don't need a duration of a day, I grab some more Dex instead.\u201c<br /> <br /> I think it heavily depends on your connectivity between rules and descriptions.<br /> If you separate them and don't try to describe things in a way to give you benefits you shouldn't have looking at the rules, then it works.<br /> If the potion brewer brews a potion to give himself a better body for a day, and he drinks it immediately after concoction, then he is equal to the meditation/prayer/yadda mage. Description: \u201cl have to drink the potion while it's still fresh.\u201c<br /> <br /> Another possible way would be to handle rules and descriptions even more separated.<br /> Both mages give themselves +2 on all physical traits for a day. They both have it for the complete day. One sips at a flask, the other meditates. Ruleswise completely the same. The differences are only for mood.<br /> <br /> The opposite way would be to use the descriptions over the rules. A potion is more powerful if you happen to have the correct one. This is so because it is more of a pain to have the right potion than to meditate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:24:52-08:00","id":1042526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzizimine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1040833#post1040833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saikou, thanks for providing an list of options, but I have a question about one of them in particular.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The root of the question comes down to what is the difference between a Wonder/Charm/Talisman/other nomenclature for enchanted item and an effect that is locked onto an object that doesn't affect the object itself in anyway, but does affect other things near it?<br /> <br /> For example, if a mage uses Force 3, Matter 3 to heat up a piece of metal and keep it heated for days at a time (appropriate to the duration), that could easily be handled as a locked effect. Granted, the mage would need to be careful that the piece of metal doesn't get too hot to deform its shape, and that whatever it is resting on or held in doesn't catch fire, but again a simple of effect. The game mechanic of that effect would be the heat that the piece of metal gives off (i.e. it keeps you warm if kept nearby, but it really hurts if held or used as a weapon).<br /> <br /> Same thing for a Matter 3 effect, locked, to make a trench coat act as better armor. The effect is to make the trench coat more durable, but the game mechanic would be a bonus to the Armor Rating of the person wearing it.<br /> <br /> Why would these work as locked effects and not need to be enchanted items? Is it because they are constant effects and not effects that activate, run their course and then die off?<br /> <br /> If so, would it not stand to reason that creating a Life 3, Matter 3 effect in a liquid that greatly assists the body's natural healing also work as a locked effect? The effect itself is distorting the liquid, but the game mechanic benefit would be the health levels gained when that liquid interacts with a wounded human body.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't work. You can use matter to turn water into Penicilin, but not into some kind of &quot;magikal healing water&quot;. Well, defending on your Paradigm, you could do a liquid with several biological uses... But it wouldn't be a super magikal healing, at best it would be some drug that acts on several biochemical points... Thing is, it wouldn't be better than a mundane drug (you could have biology 5, farmacology 5, chemistry 5, biochemestry 5, bioengeneering 5, and perhaps be the Magaiver, the Tony Stark, Iron Man of the drugs sector, but there is NO DRUG under Consensus that allows for instant regeneration).<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Ok, with your &quot;fire sword&quot; as an example.<br /> <br /> Lets do this: Forces 3, Time 4, Entropy 2.<br /> We create an effect of fire around a sword. Accumulate enough success to turn it permanent, add Time and Entropy to put a &quot;switch&quot; on the effect, to turn it on or off with a word, for by sheating/unsheating it, for a matter of conveniente.<br /> <br /> Or, I use Prime 4(3) to weave the pattern of the sword, locking a Forces 3 effect on it to make it have a fire around it.<br /> <br /> What's the difference?<br /> <br /> Well, in practical terms, not much. You can use the sword to add fire damage either way.<br /> <br /> What's the difference in mechanical and metaphysical terms: the locked effect, is an effect you made permanentement. It is simple &quot;involving&quot; the sword. Now, the talisman/artifact that you made with Prime 4, has the effect <i>as part of its own patter</i>. The sword is not activally <i>casting</i> the effect when it burns, but rather <i>releasing</i> it.<br /> <br /> About mechanics: if I use countermagik against the effect on hold, it is done; so, it I counter your sword with a permanent fire aura effect, your sword no longer can make fire. If I do the same against your sword talisman, it will put the fires off for one turn - but it will burn again on the next turn, as long as the conditions for activation were met (a word, or being unsheated, etc) because the sword would &quot;unleash&quot; it's power again, since the power is in the sword, not in the effect. To end the power of the sword permanently, I would have to destroy it's magikal properties, something that require as many successes as building it (and an equaly hard effort to &quot;undo&quot; all the etherial changes made to the object).<br /> <br /> Now, when we go to the potions problem: using Prime 2 to make a charm, the liquid is not a &quot;healing water&quot;, as a property intrinsic of the liquid itself (you can make the SAME effect using wine, an Herb extract, pure water or even gasoline or poison, thou in this last case the ressonance and bad effects of a poison would require Prime 3, more quintessence and more successes to make a healing that will also &quot;heal&quot; the negative effects of a poison... It's not smart or useful, but it could be done). The healing property is in the etherial energies storaged in the liquid - for all effects, such a potion is a Tass, and the healing property is in the quintessence &quot;solidified&quot; in the liquid, not on the liquid itself. <br /> <br /> Now, without Prime, a potion is nothing more than a <i><b>focus</b></i>. It has absolutely NO power by itself. Even when using Time 4/Entropy 2, it is only a vessel for the effect - the effect &quot;hangs around the potion&quot; waiting for a valid target and a valid trigger (the target of the effect is not the potion mind you; and the valid trigger is drinking it. When it is drunk, the target becames the person that drank it, and the effect is finally unleashed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:50:26-08:00","id":1042534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1041305#post1041305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fair point. In which case I'd add to it by saying that in order for another mage to come and provide additional healing, they'd have to meet and beat the original roll before more damage could be healed.<br /> <br /> So if Mage #1 has six levels of damage and heals four of them by rolling 2 successes. Mage #2 would be able to heal the final 2 levels of Mage #1 if they roll 4 successes (2 to meet Mage #1's roll, 1 to target non-self, and 1 to heal two bits of damage as per Damage and Duration).<br /> <br /> If, however, Mage #1 gets hurt before Mage #2 attempts the heal, then the slate is rubbed clean.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't make much sense. As the descriptions say &quot;some <i>sorcerors</i> heal, cause a little damage, and try again&quot; (the sorcerors world is probably just a mistake). That means that:<br /> <br /> - I heal 3 points. I cut the patient to cause 1 damage, and heal 3 more points.<br /> <br /> This description seems to indicate that, what limits the Mage is the momentaneous pattern of the living subject; so, a person on the brink of death, I only heal 1 point from her; after that, the new form of her pattern has been changed as much as I can... For now. Why can I heal it after one scene? Well, simple - life patterns are dynamic. After a time, the <b>pattern</b> of the subject is <b>changed</b>. The mage can't further change <i>the life pattern as it is</i>, but all he needs is that the pattern is <i>changed</i>. So, when I cut the target with a knife, I'm changing it's pattern - allowing me to do another heal. If I heal, another Mage CAN heal the target too... And that healing effectively <b>changed</b> the pattern of the target, which should allow the first Mage to heal or again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:10:19-08:00","id":1042548,"title":"","content":"About using Correspondence for &quot;witnessing&quot; your potion being drank (thus, not needing to be physically present).<br /> <br /> It CAN be done.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> You would have to do as Ambrosia said: let the effect on &quot;hold&quot; for the final Arete roll (the ritual is only finished when the potion is ingested). So, you only truly &quot;release&quot; the effect when the potion is drank.<br /> <br /> You can use Correspondence to keep &quot;witnessing&quot; the scene.<br /> <br /> But... You'll need to keep the scrying window ALWAYS OPEN. Meaning, you'll need to keep looking with Corr 2 ALL THE TIME. So, you'll need a permanent (or, as long as it takes for the target to drink) Corr 2 effect for that.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, you could use Mind 1 toghether with Corr 2, to place your attention on that scene in &quot;another mental compartiment&quot;, or even place it in a hidden place of your own mind, so you'll won't need to pay too much attention on it, like seeing things with your peripherical vision, or talking with someone ignoring the back noise around in a crowded place (and with Mind 1, you're free to focus on other things, and can be free from the penalties from keeping multiple effects. Just be careful - using this on 10 different potions will give you a severe case of pattern bleeding however).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T20:29:44-08:00","id":1043837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1039049-potion-brewing?p=1039562#post1039562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit disappointed in how most of the interpretations demand higher level spheres, I was thinking that brewing potions would be something less experienced mages would be able to do. By the time you get to Prime 4/Time 4 (as well as your primary spheres) most mages don't really need to be messing about with brewing potions as I'd expect them to create effects with far fewer Arete rolls than before. Feels like a neglected option in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have a Node which produces Tass with the appropriate Resonance (a special herb garden which is perfectly suited for a rare breed of [insert healing-related plant here], f'rinstance); that's one Background point. Take the Tass, equal amounts to the number of successes in the potion's effect. Perform a Prime 2/[Effect's Spheres] ritual. You get twice your Arete in 'doses' which perform [Effect] when anyone who believes in the potion's paradigm imbibes it, or when used in a location forgiving to that paradigm.<br /> <br /> Done.<br /> <br /> Quite doable at character generation, with the only cost being taking the &quot;make magic items&quot; Sphere at a useful level.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, make a potion out of actual Consensual materials that actually Consensually has that effect, then use some combination of Life, Spirit, and Matter to improve its quality.<br /> <br /> Note that this is what you need to make the Effect fire off at an arbitrary event on an arbitrary target. You might plausibly make a spell 'start' later than your actual casting time, I imagine, but you need to put in the duration successes to cover the <i>entire</i> time from the casting to the end of the spell, you have to set a particular target that you can 'observe' at the time of casting, and you have to put in the Spheres so that the spell can actually detect when it's supposed to transition (i.e., if it manifests fully at 6:00 Tuesday, you need Time 1 so the spell knows when it's 6:00 Tuesday). Also, it's actually active the entire time, and can hence be unwoven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}